# Eval

- bool Eval.AllowUngatedExec = true, flameeyes

  When set to false, shell_exec, exec, passthru, and system will throw a
  RuntimeException. proc_open will also throw unless the caller is listed in
  Eval.ProcOpenGatedApprovedCallers. This is checked in addition to
  Server.AllowExec.

- std::set<std::string> Eval.ProcOpenGatedApprovedCallers = {}, flameeyes

  Set of approved callers for proc_open when Eval.AllowUngatedExec is false,
  in the format ClassName::FunctionName (for methods) or FunctionName (for
  free functions). The caller is identified via stack inspection and checked
  against this list using exact matching.

- std::set<std::string> Eval.ProcOpenGatedSkipCallers = {}, flameeyes

  Set of callers to skip during stack inspection for proc_open gating.
  When the stack walk encounters a frame whose function name is in this set,
  it continues to the next frame instead of treating it as the caller.
  This is useful for transparent wrappers (e.g. FlibSL\PHP\proc_open) that
  sit between user code and the native proc_open — without skipping them,
  the gating logic would attribute the call to the wrapper instead of the
  actual calling function. Uses the same naming format as
  Eval.ProcOpenGatedApprovedCallers.

